    "evidence_text": "Additionally, we provide the evaluation results of SVM classifiers for each target on this data set, where the classifiers use unigram, bigram, and hashtag features.\n\nAfter using linguistically-motivated feature sets together with multivalued NB and SVM as the learning models, the authors conclude that they outperform two baseline approaches  .\n\nIn  , a stance-community detection approach called SCIFNET is proposed.\n\nWe also provide the evaluation results of SVM classifiers (for each target) on this data set using unigram, bigram, and hashtag features.\n\nWe have used the SVM implementation available in the Weka data mining application  where this particular implementation employs the SMO algorithm  to train a classifier with a linear kernel.\n\nOn the other hand, we should also note that SVM-based sentiment analysis systems (such as those given in  ) have been reported to achieve better F-Measure rates for the Positive sentiment class when compared with the results obtained for the Negative class.\n\nWe have also evaluated SVM classifiers\n\nthe relatively small size of our data set, the increase in the performance of the SVM classifier Target-2 is an encouraging evidence for the exploitation of hashtags in a stance detection system.\n\nAlso presented in this study are SVM classifiers (one for each target) utilizing unigram",
